<!--
  Studio — single-component viewer for `/studio/components/:name`.

  The dynamic `[name]` segment is read off the route signals in the paired
  controller.ts (`route.params.name`) and returned as the `name` scope signal,
  so the heading below shows the selected component. The full inspector (source
  panel, prop knobs, slot matrix) lands with the studio surface build-out —
  this is the real route.

  Top chrome: the <ship-nav-top> is owned by the root layout
  (`routes/_layout.sui` → `<ship-app-chrome>`). Pages compose only
  page body — the nav is declared ONCE in the layout. The bar auto-derives
  its breadcrumb trail from `location.pathname`, so this route shows the
  `/studio/components/:name` crumbs without an explicit prop.
-->
<main class="component-viewer">
  <h1 class="component-viewer-title">{name()}</h1>
  <p class="component-viewer-sub">Component viewer — source, prop knobs, and the slot matrix land with the studio surface.</p>
</main>
